Canonical Principle

The repository may become a product, standard, methodology, and commercial service layer, but commercialization must not erase:

* research provenance;
* legal uncertainty;
* version specificity;
* client confidentiality;
* professional boundaries;
* or evidence requirements.

The operating chain is:

governance
→ stewardship
→ version-control
→ license-classification
→ client-discovery
→ rights-mapping
→ professional-review
→ readiness-assessment
→ monitored-implementation
→ quality-control